# tools/al/ales_mix_witness.rish -- mix a second track: two clips sum into one, saturating (ALES3).
#
# Season: the Six-Season double-seat, Season C thread (Lotus - the creative suite) - waymark ALES - rung ALES3.
# Design read: active-designing/20260814-fill-ales3-lotus-mix-second-track.md
# Stands on: lotus/timeline.rye (ALES2) -- the Clip it mixes and the saturation it reuses (timeline.saturate, now public).
#
# lotus/mix.rye opens a DAW's second real gesture: summing two clips into one. The selftest proves: two equal-length clips
# sum sample for sample; a sum past the i16 range SATURATES rather than wraps (30000+10000 pins to +32767); a shorter track
# contributes silence past its end so the mix runs the longer length; mixing with an empty clip is identity; mix is
# commutative; and mix composes with ALES2's gain (set each track's level, then sum). Mix is total over two valid clips --
# every clip shares the one bound, so the longer length always fits. Purely local -- no network, no keys, no funds, no device.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/al/ales_mix_witness.rish

say "ales-mix: Language EN — ALES3 opens a DAW's second gesture over ALES2's clips: summing two tracks into one, sample for sample and in order."
say "ales-mix: Style Radiant — two tracks become one; the one correctness beyond a position-wise add is saturation, reused from ALES2's gain, so a loud sum never wraps to the opposite sign."
say "ales-mix: Lens TAME — bounded Clips, u32 counts, i16 samples, the sum widened to i64 before the clamp; mix is total over two valid clips (shared bound), asserted not error-guarded; siloed to lotus/, no network, no keys, no funds, no device."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "lotus/bin/mix"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p lotus/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build lotus/mix.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "ales-mix: build failed — ${build.err}"

let outfile = "lotus/bin/mix.out"
let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest > ${outfile} 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "ales-mix: selftest exited non-zero — see ${outfile}"

let shown = run ["sh" "-c" "cat ${outfile}"]
say "ales-mix: ${shown.out}"

let green = run ["sh" "-c" "grep -q 'GREEN ales-mix' ${outfile} && echo yes"]
assert (trim green.out) == "yes" else "ales-mix: selftest did not print the GREEN ales-mix line"

say "ales-mix: GREEN — two tracks mix into one, saturating rather than wrapping, a shorter track silent past its end; the next Lotus rung can clock the timeline to a real sample rate or add a fade envelope (gain that ramps)."
